 "_why": "THE KILN WYRM's arena (DESIGN24-bosses.md section 1, builder B NIGHT24): a closed room built only from axis-aligned boxes for the C# collider: 60 m across, 30 m high, the corners stepped to read as a cylinder, 4 full-height pillars, 3 floating platforms (5.5, 8.5 and 11.5 m up; reach them by the coil's rise, a wall kick or a boosted jump), 4 tall walls to kick from. Coordinates are ARENA-LOCAL (centre 0, 0, 0, floor y 0): the layer-1 builder offsets them to the boss room. The player enters at playerSpawn (the south wall, a nook the worm stays 6 m clear of); the worm emerges from the floor hole at the centre-north. Not a SurvivalMap export: no nav grid, no zones (nothing walks here but the player). Generated by a script from the same numbers as Design/bosses/wyrm.json. NIGHT26 (builder B, level 3; Tools/gen-wyrm26.py): the same room with 6 WALL-RIDE SLABS added (free-standing, 1.5 m thick, 8 m long, 13 m high, 3.25 m off the wall ring: a corridor to wall-ride along, wall-jump between slab and wall, chain from slab to pillar to platform), each placed only where it stays 3.6 m clear of every worm route (the finale's included), and one more platform. Slab positions (x, z, axis): [[-12.0, -26.0, 'x'], [-12.0, 26.0, 'x'], [-26.0, 12.0, 'z'], [12.0, -26.0, 'x'], [12.0, 26.0, 'x'], [26.0, 12.0, 'z']].",
